    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • Chinese Brand AITO Plans 2027 European Launch\nThe Perfect Nordic-Style Tiny Home Is Budget-Friendly and Big Enough for Four\n37 photos\nPhoto: Mobi House\nA natural fall landscape is the perfect backdrop for this beautiful home on wheels that embodies all the best qualities of the Nordic aesthetic, but it’s actually flexible enough to fit in everywhere. The new Mobi River has it all, from a space-efficient layout to smart utilities and stunning views, and the best part is that it’s purposely meant to be affordable.\nMobi House grew from a small business founded by husband and wife Bartek and Kasia to the largest manufacturer of mobile homes in Poland and one of the most acclaimed manufacturers in Europe. It happened in less than a decade, and it started with the tiny house that Bartek built himself and lived in for two years, while living in Norway. Scandinavian style had a huge influence on the couple and, later, on the Mobi House creations, and it’s still present today.\nAs it continued to develop and expand, the Polish brand added new lines to its already impressive portfolio, developed in direct response to specific needs or trends on the market. One of them is the Invest Line. As the name suggests, it’s geared toward investors looking to get a quick, guaranteed return on their investment. The homes in this series are purposely budget-friendly, low-maintenance, and flexible, to address the needs of beginner entrepreneurs .\nThe Invest Line homes are built to weigh no more than 3.5 tons so that they can be registered as caravans. This allows owners to install them even in remote locations, and also relocate them easily when needed. Secondly, they are built with specific damage-resistant and scratch-resistant materials, and then equipped with appliances that are easy to replace; all of this translates to low maintenance and lower costs over time.\nPhoto: Mobi House Lastly, future owners have the option to add an integrated smart system that allows the remote control of basically all the main functions of the house, from access to lighting, heating, and air conditioning, all via a simple mobile application. All of these advantages transform the Invest Line homes into the perfect package for an entrepreneur looking to start a tiny house rental business or a small hospitality business.\nMobi River is a new and an old model at the same time. It has evolved from the popular Mobi Individual design, and it has now become a permanent part of the Invest Line range, under the name of Mobi River. In a nutshell, this could be described as the perfect Nordic-style tiny house for short-term living, both for families or investors. It’s highly compact, boasting less than 20 square meters (215 square feet) of floor space, yet it can accommodate up to four people.\nThe single-loft configuration includes a flexible lounge area that can serve as a ground-floor bedroom. The design itself takes the best of the Scandinavian aesthetic and gives it a modern-classic twist. You have core elements such as the oversized picture windows for excellent views, the natural tone and texture of wood, minimal furniture for a clean, clutter-free look, and a function-follows-form approach that makes the most of a small living space.\nModular furniture is one of the signature elements introduced by the Polish brands and present in almost all of its custom-builds. It takes space efficiency to the next level while complementing the minimalist approach to interior design. In the case of Mobi River, a couple of well-picked items change the functionality of the entire space, and it works like magic.\nPhoto: Mobi House First, you have a fold-down table and a couple of fold-down chairs in the small area between the actual lounge and the main entrance. When unfolded, this becomes an excellent dining setup or even a workspace. When folded, that entire area is freed for other activities or simply for a clutter-free look. It’s as simple as that.\nAs for the lounge itself, it can be furnished either with a custom-made raised bed that hides huge storage drawers underneath and that can double as a daybed during daytime, or with a standard convertible sofa. Either way, this open space is intended to function both as a lounge during the day and a bedroom at night, which is a common feature in almost all Nordic-style tiny homes.\nThe raised bed option adds considerable storage, which can be particularly important for families looking to invest in Mobi River as a vacation home or weekender. A tiny home that’s only 6.6-meters (21.6 feet) long and 2.5-meter (8 feet) wide doesn’t typically have a lot of room left for storage, which is one of the main reasons why Mobi River isn’t offered as a long-term accommodation option. Still, clever layout makes room for storage wherever possible.\nThis includes a custom-crafted closet near the main entrance, with side storage for outerwear and shoes, and conventional storage for clothes and personal items. The kitchen comes with its own custom-made cabinetry (laminated plywood and composite materials), enough for basic storage, and the bathroom is also equipped with a compact vanity.\nPhoto: Mobi House The kitchen doesn’t take up too much space inside this layout, which is another indication that this isn’t a tiny home built for permanent accommodation. Appliances include a compact under-counter fridge, a stove/oven, a built-in dishwasher, and a range hood. The same compact, space-saving approach turns this model’s loft into a minimalist, but practical bedroom.\nIt has the structure of an attic rather than a loft, with only a tiny window in the back instead of the typical horizontal windows on each side, and only enough floor space for a two-person bed mattress. Yes, this room counts as a two-person bedroom, but don’t expect the cozy comfort or the fancy features of a luxury tiny house loft. This goes for the access as well – there’s no staircase, which would have taken up way too much space.\nThe simple movable ladder that provided access to the loft bedroom is cleverly stored on the wall near the entrance area, so that it becomes almost invisible when not in use. Style-wise, the Nordic influence is reflected in the neutral color palette and minimalist décor (including the light fixtures). Natural light and the surrounding views become part of the décor, which is something that defines Scandinavian interiors.\nThe multi-purpose lounge/bedroom in particular looks and feels stunning thanks to not one, but two enormous panoramic windows that bring the outdoors in. It’s the classic Nordic recipe for a warm and cozy ambiance and an immersive living experience in the middle of nature. This is why Mobi River works best in a natural environment, where it can become a comfortable sanctuary for a deeper connection with nature and a truly relaxing experience.\nPhoto: Mobi House Mobi River is based on a timber frame, but its interior relies heavily on laminated plywood (an affordable alternative that is also low-maintenance and durable). The thermal insulation is meant to ensure year-round comfort, and customers have multiple choices for heating, including underfloor heating and air conditioning with a heating function. The house is delivered on a Lift &Go trailer by MH Trailers, which allows the chassis to be detached from the tiny house after installation.\nA seamless blend of natural simplicity and smart, contemporary features, this tiny house takes the best of the Scandinavian aesthetic and elevates it for even better flexibility, while creating cozy comfort for up to four guests with minimal use of space.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\ncustom tiny house Mobi House tiny house tiny home\nAbout the author: Otilia Drăgan\nOtilia believes that if it’s eco, green, or groundbreaking, people should know about it (especially if it's got wheels or wings). Working in online media for over five years, she's gained a deeper perspective on how people everywhere can inspire each other. Full profile\nUP NEXT Forgotten Legends: 5 Defunct American Carmakers and Their Greatest Production Models",
